// Fake runtime module for the inclusion-machinery test (Task 4). Includes
// helper.cla so the test also covers a multi-file runtime module: expand's
// recursion into rtPath's own includes must have ALL of its heads spliced
// into the combined program, not just rtPath's own trailing head.
//
// Plan native-5d Task 1 (IR tree-shake): named rtFileSave, not an arbitrary
// probe name -- cprint.cla's IFileSave intrinsic arm always emits a call to
// the literal C symbol clar_fn_rtFileSave, regardless of which module
// actually supplies it, and shake.cla's own IFileSave arm roots that exact
// name. prog.cla's file.save call is what makes this function (and, via its
// own call below, rtIncHelper) survive shake's now-live dead-code
// elimination -- the previous "rtIncProbe" name was never actually the
// target of any call the emitted C makes (real or fake ser.cla), so it was
// always unreachable; shake now correctly drops unreachable functions,
// which broke the OLD assertions. Renaming to the real target name is the
// same fix a real (reachable) ser.cla module gets for free.
include "helper.cla"

func rtFileSave(): int {
    return rtIncHelper() + 4242
}
